import site_account_support.dl

set instance to an instance of website fixture
set view to a new UI view
set view's instance to the address of instance
set state to a new website state
set state's services to the browser UI service provider
set state's view to the address of view
set instance's state to (the address of state) as a pointer
prepare website fixture editors in (the address of state)
set stateptr to the address of state
set account to the address of (state's account)
initialize the website river in stateptr
open website progress in stateptr
open website account with (a JSON object containing [JSON text "projectId" is "demo-dynlex-games"]) in stateptr
fail account test request (account's connect request) in stateptr
require condition ((account's phase = 5) and ((the value of "Game content" in (the address of instance)) = 2)) reporting "A connection failure exposed a stored account game"
retry website account in stateptr
deliver account test reply (a new JSON value of kind the JSON null kind) to request (account's connect request) in stateptr
identify account test user (the string form of "alice") in stateptr
fail account test request (account's read request) in stateptr
require condition ((account's phase = 5) and (state's progress's profile = "guest")) reporting "A failed initial read selected an empty account save"
set account test connectivity true in stateptr
deliver account test reply (a JSON object containing [JSON child "value" is (a new JSON value of kind the JSON null kind)]) to request (account's read request) in stateptr
require condition ((account's write request != 0) and (account's phase = 4)) reporting "A missing cloud document did not initialize this account"
deliver account test reply (a JSON object containing [JSON flag "matched" is true]) to request (account's write request) in stateptr
set account test connectivity false in stateptr
edit account test plan (the string form of "offline draft") in stateptr
require condition ((account's dirty) and ((account's deadline = 0) and (account's write request = 0))) reporting "Offline edits scheduled unavailable cloud writes"
ignore follow website account action (the string form of "action:account-sign-out") in stateptr
require condition ((account's signing out = false) and (account's auth request = 0)) reporting "Offline sign-out skipped its cloud barrier"
set account test connectivity true in stateptr
require condition (account's write request != 0) reporting "Returning online did not flush local edits"
fail account test request (account's write request) in stateptr
require condition ((account's dirty) and (account's deadline != 0)) reporting "A failed write discarded progress or stopped retry scheduling"
deliver account test reply (a new JSON value of kind the JSON null kind) to request (account's deadline) in stateptr
deliver account test reply (a JSON object containing [JSON flag "matched" is true]) to request (account's write request) in stateptr
require condition (account's dirty = false) reporting "A successful retry retained dirty state"
identify account test user (the string form of "bob") in stateptr
deliver account test reply (a JSON object containing [JSON text "value" is "{corrupt cloud data"]) to request (account's read request) in stateptr
require condition ((account's phase = 5) and (state's progress's profile = "user:alice")) reporting "A damaged cloud save replaced the committed local profile"
require condition (account's write request = 0) reporting "A damaged cloud save was silently overwritten"
retry website account in stateptr
read account test cloud (the string form of "repaired bob") in stateptr
require condition ((account's phase = 4) and (state's progress's profile = "user:bob")) reporting "Retry could not load a repaired cloud save"
edit account test plan (the string form of "bob while watcher ends") in stateptr
flush website account save in stateptr
set stale to account's write request
fail account test request (account's watch request) in stateptr
require condition ((account's phase = 5) and ((account's write request = 0) and (account's watch request = 0))) reporting "A failed auth observer retained session operations"
deliver account test reply (a JSON object containing [JSON flag "matched" is true]) to request stale in stateptr
require condition (account's phase = 5) reporting "A late write re-enabled a failed auth session"
retry website account in stateptr
require condition ((account's watch request != 0) and (account's phase = 2)) reporting "Retry did not restore the auth observer"
identify account test user (the string form of "") in stateptr
require condition ((account's phase = 4) and (state's progress's profile = "guest")) reporting "The restored observer could not return to the guest profile"
require condition ((the UI value for (the control labeled "Game save status" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance))'s text = "Progress saves in this browser") reporting "A recovered account still displayed a stale error"
free website river trace the address of (state's river's trace)
free state's river's coding
free state's progress's document
free account's configuration
free account's revision
set pending to state's requests
loop while pending != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to website request):
    set next to pending's next
    deallocate pending
    set pending to next
release website fixture editors in (the address of state)
close (the address of instance)
print line "Account failures preserve committed profiles and corrupt sources; online, retry and observer recovery keep stale operations retired."
